        "section": "8.3 (Two bonds cleaved; OE+. alpha-alpha(re))"
      },
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Table 8.2 (p.167, Two bonds cleaved, OE+. alpha-alpha with H rearrangement) = the McLafferty rearrangement. Book draws 4 fishhook arcs; moves 1,2 (O+. abstracts the gamma-H) and moves 4,5 (the gamma-radical drives beta-cleavage) are drawn, move 3 (the C(gamma)-H electron staying on C(gamma)) and move 6 (the C(alpha)-C(beta) electron staying on C(alpha)) are the implicit homolysis hooks required for electron balance (not drawn). The product is drawn in the book as [.CH2-C(R')=O]+ (a distonic radical cation, radical on the former alpha-carbon); the book's box omits the O-H that the transferred gamma-H must produce, so as literally drawn it is short one H -- encoded here as the mass-balanced distonic ion [.CH2-CH=OH]+ (C2H4O), isomeric with the enol radical cation. Charge-retention channel drawn; charge migration (RHC=CH2+.) is the drawn alternative. Migrating gamma-H carried as isotope [1H:10]. Instantiation = hexanal radical cation (R'=H, R=ethyl); no m/z / intensity printed -- m/z curator-computed."
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_mech",
      "source_id": "mod_rules",
      "target_type": "mechanism",
      "target_id": "IMS8-EQT8.2n",
