        "panel": null,
        "section": "src/data_generation/rules"
      },
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "curator_note": "Chemistry-verified cross-link (same bond-order/charge/spin changes) to the MØD McLafferty pair IMS_8_7_1 (gamma-H rearrangement: ...{=}[O+.]>>...[C.]...{=}[O+][H]) then IMS_8_7_2 / IMS_8_7_3 (beta-cleavage giving alkene + enol radical cation [C]{=}[C][O+.][H]); MØD splits the concerted book scheme into rH + alpha steps and draws the enol tautomer (radical on O) rather than the distonic form (radical on C-alpha) drawn here -- the two are isomeric C2H4O+. products. Same reaction as the detailed record IMS8-EQ8.7 (also hexanal). Charge-migration channel = MØD IMS_8_7_5 (alkene radical cation [C]{=}[C+.]) / IMS_8_7_4. Not RDKit substructure-tested (DFS is a MØD reaction rule, not a SMARTS)."
    }
